; levelfacing.eval - a stair faces the way you STEP OFF it (2026-09-25), in a
; scratch copy of the demo world (run with -project lb_facing). LevelBuildTest.py
; phase 8 first rewrites that copy's crypt levels in the OLD form - every stair
; `south` (the way its steps rise), no `stairfacing arrive` marker, a
; `destfacing=` on the stairs between floors - so this is also the migration.
;
; In through crypt_gate: it lands on crypt1's exit stair at 7,7, which rises
; to the south, so the party must face NORTH. Then down crypt1's stair at 1,1
; (walked onto from 1,2, heading north): the party lands on crypt2's stair up at
; 1,1, and faces the way THAT stair faces - north too, since it was `south` in
; the old form - not the `destfacing` the old record carried. savemap writes
; both levels in the new form.
logecho on
reset
leave
discover crypt_gate
enter crypt_gate
state
pos
tp 1 2
face n
forward 1
step 2
mapinfo
pos
savemap
